    "['mpls lsr-id [ip-address]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls ldp router-id Loopback0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'mpls ldp router-id Loopback0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nmpls ldp router-id Loopback0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nIn Cisco IOS, the equivalent command to set the LSR ID is `mpls ldp router-id`, which specifies the router ID to be used for MPLS LDP. Typically, this is set to the loopback interface address (similar to Huawei's `mpls lsr-id`). The `force` keyword can optionally be added to make the change immediate. \\n\\nNote: In Cisco, the router-id is often automatically derived from the highest loopback IP, but explicitly configuring it (especially on the loopback interface) ensures consistency, just like the Huawei configuration does.\", 'trans_template': 'mpls ldp router-id Loopback0'}]]": 1,
