    "['vsi [name] [type]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'l2vpn vfi context ldp1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'l2vpn vfi context ldp1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nl2vpn vfi context ldp1\\n vpn id 1\\n neighbor 2.2.2.2 encapsulation mpls\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. \"vsi ldp1 static\" in Huawei maps to \"l2vpn vfi context ldp1\" in Cisco, which creates the VFI (Virtual Forwarding Instance) context.\\n2. The \"pwsignal ldp\" and \"vsi-id 1\" are combined into \"vpn id 1\" in Cisco.\\n3. The \"peer 2.2.2.2\" becomes \"neighbor\" with MPLS encapsulation in Cisco.\\n\\nNote: The Cisco command assumes MPLS encapsulation since the original Huawei config shows LDP signaling. Additional parameters like control-word or sequencing would need to be added if they were specified in the original configuration.', 'trans_template': 'l2vpn vfi context ldp1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'vpn id 1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'vpn id 1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nl2vpn vfi context ldp1\\n vpn id 1\\n neighbor 2.2.2.2 encapsulation mpls\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. \"vsi ldp1 static\" in Huawei maps to \"l2vpn vfi context ldp1\" in Cisco, which creates the VFI (Virtual Forwarding Instance) context.\\n2. The \"pwsignal ldp\" and \"vsi-id 1\" are combined into \"vpn id 1\" in Cisco.\\n3. The \"peer 2.2.2.2\" becomes \"neighbor\" with MPLS encapsulation in Cisco.\\n\\nNote: The Cisco command assumes MPLS encapsulation since the original Huawei config shows LDP signaling. Additional parameters like control-word or sequencing would need to be added if they were specified in the original configuration.', 'trans_template': 'vpn id 1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 2.2.2.2 encapsulation mpls', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'neighbor 2.2.2.2 encapsulation mpls', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nl2vpn vfi context ldp1\\n vpn id 1\\n neighbor 2.2.2.2 encapsulation mpls\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. \"vsi ldp1 static\" in Huawei maps to \"l2vpn vfi context ldp1\" in Cisco, which creates the VFI (Virtual Forwarding Instance) context.\\n2. The \"pwsignal ldp\" and \"vsi-id 1\" are combined into \"vpn id 1\" in Cisco.\\n3. The \"peer 2.2.2.2\" becomes \"neighbor\" with MPLS encapsulation in Cisco.\\n\\nNote: The Cisco command assumes MPLS encapsulation since the original Huawei config shows LDP signaling. Additional parameters like control-word or sequencing would need to be added if they were specified in the original configuration.', 'trans_template': 'neighbor 2.2.2.2 encapsulation mpls'}]]": 1,
    "['pwsignal [protocol]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls l2vpn signaling protocol ldp', 'parent_command': ['l2vpn vfi context ldp1'], 'root': 'l2vpn vfi context ldp1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##  \\nmpls l2vpn signaling protocol ldp  \\n##  \\n\\nAlternatively, if the context requires a more specific VPLS-focused command in Cisco:  \\n\\n##  \\nl2 vfi VFI_NAME manual  \\n vpn id 1  \\n neighbor 2.2.2.2 encapsulation mpls  \\n##  \\n\\nNote: The exact translation depends on Cisco's VPLS/PW implementation. The first option (`mpls l2vpn signaling protocol ldp`) is a direct protocol equivalent, while the second (`l2 vfi`) reflects Cisco's VFI syntax for static pseudowires. Huawei's `pwsignal ldp` enables LDP signaling for the VSI, which Cisco typically handles via global L2VPN/LDP configuration or VFI definitions.\", 'trans_template': 'mpls l2vpn signaling protocol ldp'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'l2 vfi VFI_NAME manual', 'parent_command': ['l2vpn vfi context ldp1'], 'root': 'l2vpn vfi context ldp1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##  \\nmpls l2vpn signaling protocol ldp  \\n##  \\n\\nAlternatively, if the context requires a more specific VPLS-focused command in Cisco:  \\n\\n##  \\nl2 vfi VFI_NAME manual  \\n vpn id 1  \\n neighbor 2.2.2.2 encapsulation mpls  \\n##  \\n\\nNote: The exact translation depends on Cisco's VPLS/PW implementation. The first option (`mpls l2vpn signaling protocol ldp`) is a direct protocol equivalent, while the second (`l2 vfi`) reflects Cisco's VFI syntax for static pseudowires. Huawei's `pwsignal ldp` enables LDP signaling for the VSI, which Cisco typically handles via global L2VPN/LDP configuration or VFI definitions.\", 'trans_template': 'l2 vfi VFI_NAME manual'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'vpn id 1', 'parent_command': ['l2vpn vfi context ldp1'], 'root': 'l2vpn vfi context ldp1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##  \\nmpls l2vpn signaling protocol ldp  \\n##  \\n\\nAlternatively, if the context requires a more specific VPLS-focused command in Cisco:  \\n\\n##  \\nl2 vfi VFI_NAME manual  \\n vpn id 1  \\n neighbor 2.2.2.2 encapsulation mpls  \\n##  \\n\\nNote: The exact translation depends on Cisco's VPLS/PW implementation. The first option (`mpls l2vpn signaling protocol ldp`) is a direct protocol equivalent, while the second (`l2 vfi`) reflects Cisco's VFI syntax for static pseudowires. Huawei's `pwsignal ldp` enables LDP signaling for the VSI, which Cisco typically handles via global L2VPN/LDP configuration or VFI definitions.\", 'trans_template': 'vpn id 1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 2.2.2.2 encapsulation mpls', 'parent_command': ['l2vpn vfi context ldp1'], 'root': 'l2vpn vfi context ldp1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##  \\nmpls l2vpn signaling protocol ldp  \\n##  \\n\\nAlternatively, if the context requires a more specific VPLS-focused command in Cisco:  \\n\\n##  \\nl2 vfi VFI_NAME manual  \\n vpn id 1  \\n neighbor 2.2.2.2 encapsulation mpls  \\n##  \\n\\nNote: The exact translation depends on Cisco's VPLS/PW implementation. The first option (`mpls l2vpn signaling protocol ldp`) is a direct protocol equivalent, while the second (`l2 vfi`) reflects Cisco's VFI syntax for static pseudowires. Huawei's `pwsignal ldp` enables LDP signaling for the VSI, which Cisco typically handles via global L2VPN/LDP configuration or VFI definitions.\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 2.2.2.2 encapsulation mpls'}]]": 1,
    "['vsi-id [id]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'vpn id 1', 'parent_command': ['l2vpn vfi context ldp1', 'mpls l2vpn signaling protocol ldp'], 'root': 'l2vpn vfi context ldp1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nvpn id 1\\n##', 'trans_template': 'vpn id 1'}]]": 1,
    "['peer [ip-address]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 2.2.2.2', 'parent_command': ['l2vpn vfi context ldp1', 'mpls l2vpn signaling protocol ldp'], 'root': 'l2vpn vfi context ldp1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nneighbor 2.2.2.2\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco\\'s implementation of L2VPN/VPLS using LDP signaling (similar to Huawei\\'s \"pwsignal ldp\"), the equivalent command to specify a peer LSR is typically \"neighbor\" rather than \"peer\". The functionality remains the same - it establishes a pseudowire connection to the specified peer router (2.2.2.2 in this case).', 'trans_template': 'neighbor 2.2.2.2'}]]": 1,
