    "['interface [interface-name]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1\\nencapsulation dot1Q 2\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei subinterface creation `interface GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1` is directly equivalent in Cisco\\n- The Huawei `vlan-type dot1q 2` command becomes `encapsulation dot1Q 2` in Cisco to specify 802.1Q VLAN tagging\\n- The Cisco command maintains the same subinterface numbering scheme (1.1) and VLAN ID (2) as the original Huawei configuration', 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'encapsulation dot1Q 2', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'encapsulation dot1Q 2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1\\nencapsulation dot1Q 2\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei subinterface creation `interface GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1` is directly equivalent in Cisco\\n- The Huawei `vlan-type dot1q 2` command becomes `encapsulation dot1Q 2` in Cisco to specify 802.1Q VLAN tagging\\n- The Cisco command maintains the same subinterface numbering scheme (1.1) and VLAN ID (2) as the original Huawei configuration', 'trans_template': 'encapsulation dot1Q 2'}]]": 1,
