    "['remote-mep ccm-receive mep-id [id] enable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ethernet cfm mep crosscheck mep-id 1', 'parent_command': ['ethernet cfm domain md1 level 7', 'ethernet cfm domain md1 service ma1'], 'root': 'ethernet cfm domain md1 level 7', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nethernet cfm mep crosscheck mep-id 1\\n##  \\n\\nExplanation:  \\nThe Huawei command `remote-mep ccm-receive mep-id 1 enable` enables the receiving of Continuity Check Messages (CCMs) from a remote MEP (Maintenance End Point) with ID 1. The equivalent Cisco command `ethernet cfm mep crosscheck mep-id 1` configures the local MEP to verify connectivity with the specified remote MEP ID (1) through CCM reception.', 'trans_template': 'ethernet cfm mep crosscheck mep-id 1'}]]": 1,
